hing  you may fail okay and the sooner you  realize this and the sooner you go  through this trial and process the  faster you'll be able to realize what  actually works for you what doesn't work  for you please also note that I'm  talking about this challenge as part of  your first year do not think that  whatever you feel and whatever you are  comfortable with in your first year is  going to stick through all the rest of  the three or four years of your college  life  okay so it may so happen that maybe  you're comfortable with a certain  routine uh  in your first year but that may no  longer be true as you grow older okay so  it is a very Dynamic process this  finding this best routine and and habits  which are suitable for you so you have  to be always always in this entire  journey of hostile life starting from  your first year you always have to start  adapting to the different changing  circumstances for example you may see  that some of the more experienced guys  they may have this habit of staying a  very late at night I mean they have fun  all through the afternoon and evening  and then  it is only at late at night that they  maybe do their assignments or maybe  study a little bit or whatever they they  need to do they do okay now if you do  not have that habit and you suddenly  abruptly you try to stay late at night  it is absolutely not going to work okay  your health will fail your the next day  will be a disaster okay so even if you  feel okay sometimes it may so happen  that the circumstance demands that okay  you have to go for some kind of a severe  change in your in your habits okay uh  for example uh there are a few students  who have the habit of during their plus  two while staying at home uh of waking  up very early in the morning and  studying that may not actually be  possible in Hostel life because if  everyone is awake at late into the night  and maybe they are pleasing playing some  loud music and these are realities of  host life okay may